# Implementation Plan: Local Metadata Repair and Cosma Export

The goal is to fix the project's Markdown files to satisfy Cosma's requirement for YAML frontmatter with a [title](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma_workspace/node_modules/@graphlab-fr/cosma/dist/back.cjs#3-4) field, thereby unblocking local graph generation.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This process will modify your Markdown files in the `Empresas` and `Asociaciones` folders by prepending a YAML frontmatter (if missing) to each file. This is necessary for Cosma to function.

## Proposed Changes

### [Cosma Workspace]

#### [NEW] [fix_metadata.js](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma_workspace/fix_metadata.js)
A script that will:
1. Recursively scan [.md](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/brain/eacdccd2-bfe6-41fb-a37b-a601902fac44/task.md) files in specified directories.
2. For each file, check for a YAML frontmatter.
3. If missing, generate one using the file's H1 or filename as the [title](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma_workspace/node_modules/@graphlab-fr/cosma/dist/back.cjs#3-4).
4. Prepend the frontmatter to the file.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
1. Run `node fix_metadata.js` inside `cosma_workspace`.
2. Verify a sample of files now have `--- \n title: ... \n ---` at the top.
3. Run `node force_export.js` to generate the final graph.

### Manual Verification
1. User verifies the interactive graph and chat interface in the [NotebookLM Web UI](https://notebooklm.google.com/).
